Ultra Council
=============

Ultra Council is a derivative work of **Carmack-Council** by Sam Hudson,
originally released under the MIT License.

    Original project : Carmack-Council
    Author           : Sam Hudson (github.com/SamJHudson01)
    Source           : https://github.com/SamJHudson01/Carmack-Council
    License          : MIT (see LICENSE)

What is derived and what is new
-------------------------------
Ultra Council substantially extends the original. It keeps the named-expert
council idea and several of the domain reference documents, and adds:

  - context-core   — a reusable 10-phase context-engineering pipeline that
                     every mode runs on (the original had no shared pipeline);
  - council-init   — per-project auto-tailoring of the roster and gates;
  - using-council  — session bootstrap + compaction re-bootstrap;
  - an evals harness (structural + behavioral drills).

The domain reference documents under `references/` — `security.md`,
`refactoring.md`, and the `quality-*.md` set — originate from Carmack-Council
and remain under its MIT license. Their copyright notice is preserved in
LICENSE as the MIT terms require.

Grateful acknowledgment to Sam Hudson for the original Carmack-Council.
